    "story": "The bandage took his right eye, and with it, half the world went dark. He had learned to turn his head to make up for it, and the turning had become its own small ache.\nThe pain came in waves, the way it always did after the medicine wore off, and he held himself very still against it — the way a man holds a cup too full to carry. Somewhere nearby, the war went on without asking him to join it.\nHe was not afraid of the dark. He was afraid of what the dark would mean when the bandage came off.",
