    "description": "A painterly World War II portrait of a nurse leaning over a wounded man, her hand resting on his brow as she checks him in warm, muted light. Grounded in WWII reenactment photography and historical authenticity, this World War II fine art photograph captures the quiet vigilance of the Greatest Generation at the bedside, where care is carried in a hand's patience rather than in instruments. This wartime portrait photography piece explores heroic portraits not through combat, but through the steady grace of those who tended the wounded. Part of Wayne Heim's *Facing History* fine art photography series. © Wayne Heim",
