    "description": "A painterly World War II portrait of a young soldier in a helmet and field jacket, a strap across his chest, smiling in a misty field in soft, muted light. Grounded in WWII reenactment photography and historical authenticity, this World War II fine art photograph captures the quiet optimism of the Greatest Generation in the pause before the road, where resolve is carried in a smile rather than in words. This wartime portrait photography piece explores heroic portraits not through combat, but through the steady grace of a man who keeps his humanity in the mist. Part of Wayne Heim's *Facing History* fine art photography series. © Wayne Heim",
