    "story": "She is holding on to the woman beside her, and the woman beside her is holding on to her, and the pile stays where it is because they are all doing the same thing — arms around shoulders, knees braced in the sand, laughing too hard to notice that the sea is not laughing with them.\n\nA week of orders bought this afternoon, and the sand in their skirts and boots and hair is the receipt for it — nobody minds the sand, because sand is what a beach day is made of, and the beach day is what the week was for. The sea is right behind them and will be there when the photograph is done, and the pile will come apart one pair of arms at a time, and they will stand up and shake the sand out of their skirts and go back to being five separate women until the next time somebody starts laughing.",
