    "notes": "The boots are the anchor of this frame — tall, black rubber, planted in the grass, they tell the viewer exactly who this man is before a word of the story is read. The bucket beside him and the tent canvas behind him set the scene without fuss, and the easy half-smile on his face keeps the portrait from going stern. It is a plain, honest portrait of the working man at the camp, and the kind of frame that brings a grounded, unpretentious presence to any wall it hangs on.",
