    "notes": "The box is what a collector will ask about first — a small wooden case with a brass butterfly on its lid, held with both hands as if it mattered more than the sitting itself, and Wayne Heim's painterly treatment makes the butterflies on her dress answer it, white on blue, soft against the golden backdrop. It is a portrait built on a single quiet question, and the answer is not in the frame, which is exactly why buyers will keep coming back to it. The glasses, the red lipstick, the half-smile: every detail is placed, and nothing in the frame is an accident. It hangs best where a close look is possible.",
